---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/compare/otto-vs-therapynotes/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/compare/">Compare EHRs</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">Otto vs. TherapyNotes</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="ed-compact">
        <div class="eyebrow">Otto vs. TherapyNotes</div>
        <h1>
          Make the next step
          <br />
          part of the same workflow.
        </h1>
        <p>
          If you are considering a TherapyNotes alternative, look at the whole
          visit. Otto connects preparation, documentation, chart review, and
          payment around the work of independent mental health care.
        </p>
        <div class="ed-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/demo/#watch">
            See the Otto workflow ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#comparison">
            Compare the details ↓
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Why consider Otto</span>
            <h2>Follow the work through to the next step.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Otto’s central idea is a connected practice day: useful context
            before the visit, documentation you review, and a clear path into
            the chart and payment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>The context comes with you</h3>
            <p>
              Patient summaries and last-session highlights connect preparation
              to the documented history.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>The note moves the work forward</h3>
            <p>
              After signature, Otto proposes structured chart updates and
              carries the visit into charge review.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Clinical changes need your approval</h3>
            <p>
              Review the note, then confirm or dismiss the proposed diagnoses,
              plan items, and medication changes.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section" id="comparison">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The features in context</span>
            <h2>Bring your practice requirements.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Include the way you document, the visits you run, and how you get
            paid. Compare each product against the same everyday work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table
            class="ed-table"
            aria-label="Otto and TherapyNotes workflow comparison"
          >
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">What to compare</th>
                <th scope="col">Otto</th>
                <th scope="col">TherapyNotes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">The visit workflow</th>
                <td>
                  Connects preparation, SOAP or DAP documentation, approved
                  chart changes, and cash-pay collection.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Provides a mental health practice platform with scheduling,
                  documentation, telehealth, and insurance workflows.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">AI documentation and preparation</th>
                <td>
                  Audio-based SOAP and DAP drafts plus patient summaries and
                  last-session highlights.
                </td>
                <td>
                  TherapyFuel includes progress-note drafting, Scribe,
                  treatment-plan generation, and Session Assist for preparation.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Clinician review</th>
                <td>
                  Review and sign the note, then confirm or dismiss proposed
                  clinical updates to the patient record.
                </td>
                <td>
                  TherapyFuel documentation can be reviewed, revised, and
                  finalized by the clinician.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Insurance needs</th>
                <td>
                  Confirm current support before choosing Otto for an
                  insurance-dependent practice. This preview describes cash-pay
                  collection.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Documents electronic claims, eligibility, and ERAs, with
                  transaction charges.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Published pricing</th>
                <td>
                  Advertises $99/month after trial; confirm billing unit, usage,
                  and additional charges.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Solo is listed at $69/month; group starts at $79 plus $50 per
                  additional clinician. TherapyFuel is $40 per enabled clinician
                  per month.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Moving your records</th>
                <td>
                  Confirm import formats, record categories, timing, and
                  assistance before scheduling a move.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Review export categories and download options before closing
                  an account. Preserve access to the original records.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-source-list">
          <p>
            Sources checked October 16, 2026. Features, plan eligibility, and
            terms can change. Confirm requirements directly with each vendor.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto product overview</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://support.therapynotes.com/hc/en-us/articles/30661380110747-TherapyNotes-Pricing-and-Subscription-Options">
                TherapyNotes subscription options
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://support.therapynotes.com/hc/en-us/articles/34844327115291-TherapyFuel-Overview">
                TherapyFuel features
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://support.therapynotes.com/hc/en-us/articles/30661278579227-Download-and-Print-Notes">
                TherapyNotes document downloads
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-choice">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">A considered move</span>
            <h2>Look at the work you want to make easier.</h2>
            <p>
              For a solo, self-pay practice, try Otto’s connected visit from
              preparation through collection. If insurance workflows are central
              to your practice, establish the required claims capabilities
              before making a decision.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ed-choice-links">
            <a href="/switch/from-therapynotes/">
              <strong>Plan your move from TherapyNotes ↗</strong>
              <span>
                Prepare exports, confirm import requirements, and check a
                sample.
              </span>
            </a>
            <a href="/tools/ehr-cost-calculator/">
              <strong>Compare software costs ↗</strong>
              <span>
                Model your own usage and the fees that apply to your practice.
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Does TherapyNotes also offer AI documentation?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. TherapyFuel includes note drafting, Scribe, revision
              features, treatment-plan generation, and preparation support.
              Confirm the exact note types and visit eligibility you need.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What should I test in Otto?</summary>
            <p>
              Follow a fictional visit through preparation, note review and
              signature, chart-update confirmation, and payment review. Evaluate
              the handoffs as well as the draft itself.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is Otto less expensive?</summary>
            <p>
              Total cost depends on your plan, users, optional features, and
              transactions. Otto’s billing unit and complete fee schedule need
              confirmation. Use the{" "}
              <a href="/tools/ehr-cost-calculator/">calculator</a> with verified
              quotes.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I keep access to my records while switching?</summary>
            <p>
              Agree on exports, retention, access, and a cutover plan with both
              vendors. Do not close the old account until the responsible
              practice owner has accepted the transition.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
